.nh
.TH "PB-SEND-CANCEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-send-cancel - Cancel a file transfer batch


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb send cancel <transfer-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Cancel a file transfer batch

.PP
Cancel an outgoing transfer by its exact transfer ID, optionally selecting a machine with --on. Cancellation reports the resulting batch state; already delivered files are not silently deleted.

.PP
Send publishes a batch to a machine's Paperboat Inbox. Completion means the receiver verified and recorded the files; status and cancel act on a transfer ID. A default destination can be set separately, while --to chooses one for the current send.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for cancel

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--on\fP=""
	destination machine name or ID

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	terminal session ID for destination context


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-send(1)\fP
